  "id": "Compound::DB00373 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Timolol is linked to Cyp2c19 through a series of molecular and pharmacological interactions. The evidence suggests that Timolol, through its effects on beta-adrenergic receptors, indirectly influences Cyp2c19 via Metoprolol or Propranolol, both of which are beta-adrenergic antagonists. This pathway highlights a recurring mechanism where the effects of Timolol are mediated through the activation of beta-adrenergic receptors, leading to the upregulation or modulation of Cyp2c19 expression. The lowest common ancestors of Timolol and its target compounds—such as Organic Cyclic Compounds and Beta-Adrenergic Antagonists—suggest a shared pharmacological profile that may underpin the observed interactions. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of beta-adrenergic signaling in linking Timolol to Cyp2c19, emphasizing a potential dependency on adrenergic modulation for the drug's metabolic effects.",
